# Rivalry results popup reference, 2026-10-26

The owner's supplied popup replaces the earlier centered laurel summary. The weekly page remains intact beneath it. The new reference explicitly adds Continue to next week inside the popup, superseding the earlier popup-only dismissal requirement; the existing main-screen Continue remains.

RSR01: A gold-framed dark sheet has a separated header, left-aligned place/award/player banner, oversized two-digit actual rank, original vector trophy/checker details and a diagonal divider. The comparison row shows the actual player's points and small native vehicle preview, a signed lead badge, and runner-up points. Podium, ordinary, unranked and shared championships retain their true title/rank; a joint winner compares against a co-leader rather than claiming an exclusive lead. The Perfect Week marker still requires five outright contested victories.

RSR02: The three lower cards show final position, contested track victories and personal bests. Personal bests use the validated distinct `personal_best_slots` count, including zero; the design's example values are not hardcoded. The opponent is the first other driver in the authoritative standings, so non-winners compare against the leader. The miniature uses the existing ProfileCar studio with the actual event vehicle, local paint, parts and condition, one owned static viewport and its existing bounded preparation. No camera, model or shared profile source changes are made.

RSR03: View results, close and Escape only dismiss. Initial keyboard focus is View results; Enter dismisses there. Explicitly focusing Continue and pressing Enter, or clicking Continue, invokes the existing adapter's scoped acknowledgement/enrollment flow once. A valid click marks the summary reviewed and closes it before the request; main Continue remains disabled while that request runs. Failure returns to the same completed weekly view with the existing error and retry. Retry reuses the original operation key. Stale accounts/memberships, background busy state and changed final payloads cannot advance a week from the sheet. No automatic dismissal acknowledges or enrolls.

RSR04/R01: The 880x540 reference composition stays together on resize and fits the viewport without a popup scrollbar. Header/date, typography, comparison, all three cards, Perfect Week marker and all three button targets are checked against actual bounds. A separate Latin display face avoids tall fallback line metrics; translated or user text requiring other scripts retains the shared font coverage. Existing catalogue translations are reused, with English fallback for new or previously uncatalogued phrases. Owner translation/appearance/touch acceptance remains.

